+# Specialty Directory Assembled in a Read Model
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The veterinarian directory answers which specialties a veterinarian holds. `REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001` asks the inverse and also lists a specialty no veterinarian holds.
+
+The association is unidirectional. `Vet` maps a many-to-many set of `Specialty`, and `Specialty` maps nothing back. No repository reads specialties, so a specialty no veterinarian holds is unreachable from the veterinarian side.
+
+The pattern catalog admits no business rule in a web controller, and this project has no service layer — see [Feature-Package Organization Without a Service Layer](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md).
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Inverse JPA mapping** — give `Specialty` a mapped-by collection of veterinarians and read it through a new repository.
+2. **Grouping in the controller** — read specialties and veterinarians, then group them inside the controller method.
+3. **Read model over two repository reads** — a specialty repository, the cached veterinarian read, and an immutable value object joining them.
+
+## Decision
+
+We take option 3. A `SpecialtyDirectory` value object in the `vet` package exposes a static factory over the two collections. It joins on the stored specialty identifier and fixes the presentation order.
+
+Option 1 needs an eager inverse collection, because open sessions are not held across rendering. That makes `Vet` and `Specialty` mutually eager, reaches back into the serialized veterinarian route, and turns a lookup value into a second aggregate root.
+
+Option 2 adds a new rule to a controller. The catalog forbids it, and the deviation this codebase already carries does not extend to new rules.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The directory's behavior is unit-testable without Spring. That includes the specialty no veterinarian holds, a case the seed data does not contain.
+- `Specialty` stays a lookup value carrying no collection, and the serialized veterinarian route is unchanged.
+- The page issues one uncached specialty read per request. The veterinarian read stays on the existing vet cache, so no new cache is declared.
+- The join is by stored identifier rather than by object equality, since `BaseEntity` overrides neither `equals` nor `hashCode`.
+- A second read model of this kind would repeat the shape rather than share an abstraction with this one.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md#contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the contracts realizing this decision
+- [Feature-Package Organization Without a Service Layer](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md) — the absent service layer this decision works within
+- [Relational Persistence via Spring Data JPA with Mapping on the Domain Types](2026-07-31-relational-persistence-with-spring-data-jpa.md) — the mapping style the rejected option would extend
