+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-specialtydirectory-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes its specialties, answering the inverse of the veterinarian directory: which veterinarians hold a given specialty (confirmed 2026-08-15). Every specialty the clinic knows is listed under its stored name, with the veterinarians holding it named in full — first name, then last name `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]`. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on the page, which lists specialties rather than the whole roster. The page is reachable by its own address alone; nothing in the system leads a reader to it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed under its stored name, all on a single page.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each of those veterinarians is named by first name followed by last name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is not shown anywhere on it.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given any page of the system, when it is rendered, then it carries no entry or link leading to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, shown as held by none.
+2. The specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. The page carries the navigation every page carries, as `REQ-SYS-001` requires; it gains no entry of its own.
+
